From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emilwojcik93 <adminit@adar.pl>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:02:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] posture: track per-client posture state and display sizes

The size policy is stateless. The host also has to remember, per client, what
posture was last launched, what size the policy wants, and what size the
virtual display was actually created with, so that a later resume can tell
whether the display must be recreated and a running stream can accept runtime
posture updates.

Add src/posture_state.* with:

- the desired size a display backend reads by display GUID when it creates the
  display, and the applied size recorded after the driver accepted it;
- the touch-size-boundary test (no size versus some size): a change between two
  touch classes is not a change, because they all get the same diagonal;
- runtime updates for a streaming client with a one second rate limit and a
  display_change verdict, plus a status view for the web UI.

Still no caller, so no behaviour change. Unit tests cover the registry, the
boundary rule and the rate limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
